# Rust build output
/target

# Anything under .local/ is scratch space: design notes, experiments, throwaway
# scripts. It is never part of the published project.
.local/

# Runtime state that must never be committed.
#
# The session file is a live credential: anyone holding it is logged into the
# account. `TGFWD_HOME=. tgfwd login` — or any variant of it while testing —
# writes the whole profile into the working directory, so the names matched here
# are the ones `Paths::from_root` actually produces: `config.toml` at the root,
# `data/session.json`, and a `cache/` of snapshotted media.
#
# Matching the real names matters more than it looks. An earlier version of this
# file listed `*.session.json`, which matches `something.session.json` and not
# the `session.json` this tool writes — so the one file that must never be
# committed was the one file not covered.
session.json
*.session
/config.toml
/data/
/cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store
